---
// Two small conceptual sketches of where a clipping element sits in a
// circuit: to ground (shunt) versus inside a feedback loop. These are
// simplified boxed signal-path sketches, not real schematics — restraint,
// per CLAUDE.md's rule on not asserting specific circuit accuracy.
---

<div class="position-diagrams">
  <figure class="position-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 140 90" role="img" aria-label="Clipping element wired to ground, shunting signal above a threshold to earth.">
      <line x1="10" y1="30" x2="130" y2="30" class="wire" />
      <circle cx="10" cy="30" r="2.5" class="node" />
      <circle cx="130" cy="30" r="2.5" class="node" />
      <line x1="70" y1="30" x2="70" y2="60" class="wire" />
      <path d="M 62 60 L 78 60 M 62 66 L 78 66 M 62 72 L 78 72" class="ground" />
      <rect x="58" y="42" width="24" height="14" class="element" />
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="position-label">Clipping to ground</span>
      <span class="position-description">The element shunts signal above a threshold to earth — a simple limiter on the path.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure class="position-card bench-module">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 140 90" role="img" aria-label="Clipping element inside a feedback loop around an amplifying stage.">
      <line x1="10" y1="45" x2="45" y2="45" class="wire" />
      <rect x="45" y="30" width="30" height="30" class="element" />
      <line x1="75" y1="45" x2="130" y2="45" class="wire" />
      <path d="M 105 45 L 105 20 L 55 20 L 55 30" class="wire feedback" fill="none" />
      <rect x="88" y="12" width="26" height="14" class="element" />
      <circle cx="10" cy="45" r="2.5" class="node" />
      <circle cx="130" cy="45" r="2.5" class="node" />
    </svg>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="position-label">Clipping in a feedback loop</span>
      <span class="position-description">The element sits around an amplifying stage, so the curve it produces depends on the loop gain too.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<style>
  .position-diagrams {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(11rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .position-card {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .position-card svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .wire {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .feedback {
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
  }

  .node {
    fill: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  .element {
    fill: var(--at-bg);
    stroke: var(--at-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .ground {
    stroke: var(--at-text-secondary);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }

  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .position-label {
    font-family: var(--bench-readout, var(--at-font-mono));
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--at-text);
  }

  .position-description {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-xs);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
</style>
